marie: opened PR 5712 with a tracehook v2 migration note + dashboard panel example. need eyes on the Rust + TS snippets and a quick link sweep: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/5712
rob: taking Rust, will run the snippet in a container.
sai: i'll do TS and screenshots.
marie: rust snippet included is:
```rust
use redwood::Client;
let client = Client::new(std::env::var("REDWOOD_KEY")?);
let mapping = client.trace().map_keys("svc-").await?;
println!("{} keys", mapping.len());
```
rob: tiny issue: need tokio runtime and explicit error handling in example. propose:
```rust
#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
  let client = redwood::Client::new(std::env::var("REDWOOD_KEY")?);
  let mapping = client.trace().map_keys("svc-").await?;
  println!("{} keys", mapping.len());
  Ok(())
}
```
rob: i'll push the patch.
sai: TS snippet looked fine but used old param name 'traceKey'  needs 'trace_key'. updating and switching to async/await pattern.
sai: updated snippet to:
```ts
import Redwood from '@redwoodai/sdk';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY });
(async () => {
  const mapping = await client.trace.mapKeys({ prefix: 'svc-' });
  console.log(Object.keys(mapping).length);
})();
```
